  "narration": "Every eye has a blind spot, but your brain hides it from you. At the back of the retina, the optic nerve exits through a tiny area with no light-sensing cells. Anything landing there creates a real gap in the image. Yet you never see a black hole. Information from the other eye and the surrounding pattern helps your visual system fill in what is missing. Close one eye and use a blind-spot test, and an object can appear to vanish. Your vision is not a camera. It is a prediction your brain keeps updating.",
